[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564106219","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100864#issuecomment-2564106219","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100864","id":2564106219,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y1Sfr","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-28T00:01:32Z","updated_at":"2024-12-28T00:01:32Z","body":"Does using `QueueFree` work? This isn't safe use of `Free` AFAIK ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564106219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564176932","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100864#issuecomment-2564176932","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100864","id":2564176932,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y1jwk","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-28T04:43:10Z","updated_at":"2024-12-28T04:43:10Z","body":"> Does using `QueueFree` work? This isn't safe use of `Free` AFAIK\n\nI concur. This is not safe use of Free. One would always want to use QueueFree instead of Free there.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564176932/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564426446","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100864#issuecomment-2564426446","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100864","id":2564426446,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y2grO","user":{"login":"AdamLearns","id":60950402,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTUwNDAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60950402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns","html_url":"https://github.com/AdamLearns","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-28T20:10:22Z","updated_at":"2024-12-28T20:10:22Z","body":"> Does using QueueFree work? This isn't safe use of Free AFAIK\n\nYes, `QueueFree()` works, and I'll switch my code to that.\n\nI think it may be worth adding some context here. I only recognized that this was unsafe usage after witnessing a crash. However, it still took me a few hours to create the minimal repro. It was difficult to pinpoint because:\n\n- It wasn't my code directly accessing the freed node.\n  - To add to this, I'm not super familiar with the Godot code itself, so despite looking through it and trying to log from various points, the `dylib` stuff threw me off.\n- When it _is_ my code accessing the freed node, I get `ERROR: System.ObjectDisposedException: Cannot access a disposed object.`\n- The crash only happens every so often.\n\nI'm not trying to argue that this should result in a _code_ fix, but perhaps [this documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_object.html#class-object-method-free) could be clearer? Maybe an extra line like \"When Godot tries to access a freed node, it may even result in a crash.\" Then again, this issue will now exist as a reference point for anyone searching for this in the future.\n\nAnyway, thank you for the prompt response!\n\nP.S. out of curiosity, why is `GridMapEditorPlugin::~GridMapEditorPlugin()` in the middle of that stack trace? The existence of that in input-related code perplexed me.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564426446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564441837","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100864#issuecomment-2564441837","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100864","id":2564441837,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y2kbt","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-28T20:45:27Z","updated_at":"2024-12-28T20:45:27Z","body":"> I'm not trying to argue that this should result in a _code_ fix, but perhaps [this documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_object.html#class-object-method-free) could be clearer? Maybe an extra line like \"When Godot tries to access a freed node, it may even result in a crash.\" Then again, this issue will now exist as a reference point for anyone searching for this in the future.\n\nHeck, I'd be in favor of just removing API access to Free. As in, making it an internal thing only. There is no real world scenario where a game/application designer using Godot would need to use a direct Free instead of a QueueFree. C# is managed code, GDScript is interpreted. Both consequently not in a position to have as much free control over freeing a node as a direct Free offers.\n\nSo, yeah, documentation clarification is the least we should consider. Fully agreeing with you there.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564441837/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]